<Base
  title="Disclaimer | Chip & Cell"
  description="Chip & Cell is a data and research site, not an advisory service. What that means in practice, and what our numbers can and cannot tell you."
>
  <h1>Disclaimer</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: September 21, 2026</p>

  <h2>No investment advice</h2>
  <p>
    Chip &amp; Cell publishes data and written analysis about 27 listed Korean semiconductor
    and battery companies. None of it is personalised investment advice. We do not know your
    finances, your tax position, your time horizon or your risk tolerance, and nothing here
    is tailored to them. We are not a licensed investment adviser, broker-dealer or
    financial planner.
  </p>

  <h2>Where the numbers come from, and how they fail</h2>
  <p>
    Stock pages are refreshed by an automated pipeline after each Seoul session close, using
    KRX market data and public company filings. Automated pipelines fail in specific ways:
    a feed goes stale and yesterday's close is shown as today's; a ticker is reorganised
    after a split or merger and history breaks; a filing is restated after we have already
    published from the first version. We correct what we catch, but we cannot promise the
    figure in front of you is right. Always check a primary source before acting.
  </p>

  <h2>Model-assisted writing</h2>
  <p>
    Deep dives and weekly reviews are drafted with model assistance on top of the collected
    data, then reviewed before publishing. Review catches most errors, not all of them.
    Treat our interpretation as one reading of the data, not as fact. The
    <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> sets out what is computed and what is
    inferred.
  </p>

  <h2>Forward-looking statements</h2>
  <p>
    Anything about future demand, capacity, pricing or margins is opinion about an unknown
    future, not a forecast you should rely on. Semiconductor and battery cycles in
    particular turn faster than most coverage of them.
  </p>

  <h2>No compensation from covered companies</h2>
  <p>
    We accept no payment, equity, product or other consideration from any company we cover,
    and we do not run sponsored posts or paid links inside our coverage. The site carries
    third-party display advertising, which is sold and placed by Google — those advertisers
    have no say in what we write and no advance sight of it. See our
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for how that advertising uses cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided "as is". To the fullest extent permitted by law, we accept no
    liability for any loss arising from the use of, or reliance on, anything published here.
  </p>
</Base>

